-- Q_s
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='When dimensioning continuous-flow gravity thickeners, the required surface $A_{\text {thickener }}\left[\mathrm{m}^{2}\right]$ is calculated by the added sludge quantity $Q_{\mathrm{s}}\left[\mathrm{m}^{3} / \mathrm{h}\right]$, the influent solids content $T S S_{\text {IN }}\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} / \mathrm{m}^{3}\right]$ and the solids loading rate SLR $\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} /\left(\mathrm{m}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{~d}\right)\right]$ selected from Table 1. — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2, printed p.16-17) [VC] — unit m3/h confirmed verbatim. DIMENSIONAL FINDING: with Q_s in m3/h and SLR in kgTSS/(m2.d) the printed Eq.2 yields m2*d/h, not m2 — see the Eq.2 note and the STAGED file.', verified_at=now() where id='d5c7970a-a3fa-4df7-a013-ce27c641eb4f' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- TSS_In
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='the influent solids content $T S S_{\text {IN }}\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} / \mathrm{m}^{3}\right]$ and the solids loading rate SLR $\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} /\left(\mathrm{m}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{~d}\right)\right]$ selected from Table 1. | $T S S_{\text {In }}$ & {$[\mathrm{gTSS} / \mathrm{l}]$} & Influent total suspended solids — printed p.16-17 and p.7-8', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 + §2.1.10 symbol legend, printed p.16-17 and p.7-8) [VC] — the guideline declares this symbol in TWO units: kgTSS/m3 (§4.1.2) and gTSS/l (§2.1.10 legend and the §2.2 table). They are numerically identical (1 kg/m3 = 1 g/l); the encoding uses kgTSS/m3 here and gTSS/l on M381E-08. No conversion defect.', verified_at=now() where id='6120d83b-264a-4e18-8888-90e0ffa4c99b' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- TS_percent
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='For determination of the solids content, the total solids concentration (\% TS) and the concentration of total suspended solids (gTSS/l) are analysed according to DIN EN 12880 [5]. | For simplification, the solids-related degree of separation of a gravity thickener or a mechanical thickening device is calculated by converting the total solids content in \% TS to gTSS/l by multiplication with a factor of 10 ( $1 \% \mathrm{TS}=10 \mathrm{gTSS} / \mathrm{l}$ ) without regarding the differences in density. — printed p.7-8', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.1.9 + §2.1.10, printed p.7-8) [VC] — the 1 %TS = 10 gTSS/l conversion is printed and is the bridge between this field and TSS_In / TSS_Dis; it is NOT encoded as an equation. Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='1f2f5c87-485d-490d-943f-9fdf3298a5f5' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- water_content
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Before thickening, the water content of sewage sludges varies between approx. $96 \%$ and 99,5 \% depending on their origin. The reason for the high water content of sewage sludges and the correspondingly required technical effort for sludge thickening is the high water binding capacity of sewage sludges. — printed p.8', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.1.11, printed p.8) [VC] — 96 % to 99,5 % is a descriptive typical band ("varies between approx."), not a requirement; correctly NOT gated.', verified_at=now() where id='fcad88e0-25b6-4949-bdc0-238dfe815111' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- temperature
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Figure 3: Influence of solids content and temperature on the viscosity (apparent viscosity) of primary and waste activated sludge [21] | $T$ & T & ${ }^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ & Temperature — printed p.12 and p.9', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§3.2 Fig.3 + §2.2 symbol table, printed p.12 and p.9) [VC] — the temperature dependency itself is only shown graphically (Fig.3, Fig.7); the md carries the figures as image links, so no numeric values are readable from the transcript.', verified_at=now() where id='c00b4dfa-7ad8-49b4-a4dc-ea26d9a3487c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- apparent_viscosity
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Things are different for mechanical thickening of waste activated sludge, especially if centrifuges without the addition of flocculants are used. Then apparent viscosity increases significantly [22]. | In order to prevent operational problems, viscosity shall be taken into consideration for friction loss in pipes, selection of pumps for the conveyance of thickened sludge and for the design of agitation devices in sludge stabilisation plants. — printed p.11-13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§3.2, printed p.11-13) [VC] — unit mPa.s per the §2.2 symbol table (p.9). This is one of the few genuine "shall" obligations in the leaflet, but it obliges a CONSIDERATION, not a numeric limit, so no numeric gate is defensible. Staged as an attestation candidate.', verified_at=now() where id='81987692-37f2-4299-9484-98981769a660' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- EC
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='In wastewater treatment technology, salt concentration can be estimated using the parameter electrical conductivity. | EC & LF & mS/cm or S/m & Electrical conductivity — printed p.7-8 and p.9', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.1.9 + §2.2 symbol table, printed p.7-8 and p.9) [VC] — UNIT FINDING: the guideline declares this symbol in TWO units that are NOT numerically identical ("mS/cm or S/m"; 1 S/m = 10 mS/cm). The encoded unit mS/cm is one of the two printed options; a value entered in S/m would be off by a factor 10. Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='e539d79f-fb0d-473c-8278-b8c2377a1f01' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- thickenability_class
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='According to their characteristics - especially in regard to their water binding capacity - sludges are generally classified into three groups: | Easily thickenable/dewaterable sludges | Averagely thickenable/dewaterable sludges | Hardly thickenable/dewaterable sludges — printed p.8-9', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.1.12, printed p.8-9) [VC] — the three encoded enum values are the three printed group names verbatim. Note the leaflet uses a SECOND, differently worded three-way split in Tab.1 ("hardly / averagely / easily settleable"), which is what the SLR selection actually keys on; the encoding merges the two. Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='d5bcb060-104c-420a-be56-cbd3dbf825bf' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- beta_value
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Activated sludge from the biological treatment step, trickling filter sludge, hydroxide sludges from electroplating plants or pickling plants, phosphate precipitation sludges with a $\beta$-value (mol precipitant/mol phosphorus) significantly above 1,5. | $\beta$-value & $\beta$-Wert & - & Spec. phosphate precipitant demand mol metal/mol P — printed p.9', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.1.12 group 3 + §2.2 symbol table, printed p.9) [VC] — "significantly above 1,5" is a soft classification threshold inside a descriptive list, not a limit; correctly NOT gated.', verified_at=now() where id='bc304c68-6290-446e-8fc3-4aae0cd9190e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

