-- H_R
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='A minimum height of $0,3 \mathrm{~m}$ or a height equal to the height of the scraper blade shall be assumed for the raking zone $H_{\mathrm{R}}$. — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2, printed p.16-17) [VC] — genuine "shall". Gate CR-005 (H_R >= 0.3) matches the printed minimum and its boundary is inclusive, as printed. The printed ALTERNATIVE branch ("a height equal to the height of the scraper blade") has no encoded field, so the effective max(0,3 m; blade height) reading cannot be enforced. Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='0600dd65-d309-46af-a97b-48b67ae22b8f' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- A_thickener
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='When dimensioning continuous-flow gravity thickeners, the required surface $A_{\text {thickener }}\left[\mathrm{m}^{2}\right]$ is calculated by the added sludge quantity $Q_{\mathrm{s}}\left[\mathrm{m}^{3} / \mathrm{h}\right]$, the influent solids content $T S S_{\text {IN }}\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} / \mathrm{m}^{3}\right]$ and the solids loading rate SLR $\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} /\left(\mathrm{m}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{~d}\right)\right]$ selected from Table 1. — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 Eq.2, printed p.16-17) [VC] — output of Eq.2. ORPHAN NOTE: no gate and no downstream equation consumes A_thickener; it is the terminal design output of the gravity worksheet.', verified_at=now() where id='6fd3a50a-1d78-4420-9a29-5c6da5c20ca5' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- H_S
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The height of the sludge zone $H_{\mathrm{S}}[\mathrm{m}]$ is calculated using the solids loading rate SLR [kgTSS/ $\left(\mathrm{m}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{~d}\right)$ ], the solids content of the thickened sludge $\operatorname{TSS}_{\text {thick }}\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} / \mathrm{m}^{3}\right]$, and the detention time $t_{\mathrm{d}}[\mathrm{d}]$ of the sludge in the sludge zone: — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 Eq.3, printed p.16-17) [VC] — output of Eq.3, consumed by gate CR-006 (H >= H_W + H_S + H_R). Dimensional check closes: kg/(m2.d) * d / (kg/m3) = m.', verified_at=now() where id='8d07d0dd-99e7-4db2-9dd7-f96340d20d50' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- H_W
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='For the supernatant zone a height $H_{\mathrm{w}}$ of about 1.0 m is necessary. — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2, printed p.16-17) [VC] — the printed value is "about 1.0 m is necessary", i.e. approximate; gate CR-004 enforces it as a hard floor H_W >= 1.0. Note the leaflet prints "1.0" with a DOT here although its own §2.2 note states "A comma is used as a decimal sign" and every neighbouring value uses a comma (0,3 m). Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='73a7c2b5-9c8a-44c0-9990-3e00b2c62ccc' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- H
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The total height of the con-tinuous-flow gravity thickener thus amounts to $H=H_{\mathrm{W}}+H_{\mathrm{S}}+H_{\mathrm{R}}$, measured at the outer circumference of the thickener. | H & H & m & Total height of the continuous flow thickener ( $H=H_{\mathrm{W}}+H_{\mathrm{s}}+H_{\mathrm{R}}$ ) — printed p.16-17 and p.9', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 + §2.2 symbol table, printed p.16-17 and p.9) [VC] — the print gives an EQUALITY; the encoding holds it only as gate CR-006 (H >= sum) with no equation row, so H stays hand-enterable although it is fully derived (the #22 class). Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='7cabaf87-9e49-4903-a0ea-41dfa934bb11' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- floor_slope
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Continuous-flow gravity thickeners with mechanical sludge removal equipment have sloped floors, similar to round primary sedimentation tanks, with a slope of possible more than 1,7 in 1 (according to DIN 19552 [6]) and a central sludge hopper. | Thickeners which are not equipped with scrapers generally are emptied sufficiently at a floor slope above 60 degrees. — printed p.15 and p.14', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 + §4.1.1, printed p.15 and p.14) [VC] — UNIT FINDING: the guideline states this one quantity in TWO different dimensions — a RATIO ("more than 1,7 in 1", continuous thickeners) and an ANGLE ("above 60 degrees", batch thickeners without scrapers). The single encoded field (unit "-") cannot hold both. Also the continuous value is permissive ("a slope of possible more than"), not a "shall". Gate CR-016 is presence-only. Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='7ec3ddc5-f380-4398-8268-dd6829bf7b75' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- sludge_interface_level
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='For the operation of a continuous flow thickener the most important parameter is the sludge interface. It defines the detention time of the solids in the sludge zone and thus achievable total solids concentration. | Measuring systems up to a measuring range of 30 m are available. Measuring signals can be calibrated in a range of ca. $0,3 \%$ up to ca. $10 \%$ total solids content in the sludge or in the suspension. — printed p.17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2.1, printed p.17) [VC] — the 30 m / 0,3 %-10 % figures describe available INSTRUMENT ranges, not a design limit; correctly NOT gated.', verified_at=now() where id='a42afe26-aebe-4614-bb3c-966cf7ac6575' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- t_d
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='For raw sludges a detention time or mean cell residence time of no more than 1,5 days should be chosen, since otherwise formation of biogas interferes with the settling process. — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2, printed p.16-17) [VC] — the value 1,5 d and the inclusive boundary of gate CR-003 (t_d <= 1.5) both match the print. TWO gate findings: the modal is "should" (block anchored on soft text), and the printed scope is "For raw sludges" only while CR-003 fires for every sludge type. §6.1.2 additionally prints "thickening time may range between one and two days". Staged.', verified_at=now() where id='f570547c-539a-434d-808f-c91618a3e4fa' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- SLR
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Table 1: Dimensioning parameters for continuous-flow gravity thickeners | Settling characteristics of the sludge & Type of sludge & Solids loading rate SLR [kg TSS/(m².d)] | hardly settleable & waste activated sludge & 20-50 | averagely settleable & mixed primary sludge, digested sludge & 40-80 | easily settleable & primary sludge, mineral sludges, non-digestible sludges & up to 100 | The solids loading rate shall be smaller than the particle settling velocity of the sludge solids. — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 Tab.1, printed p.16-17) [VC] — SR-2: Tab.1 is a RANGE table keyed on settleability, so the point value must stay an explicit engineer selection. GATE FINDING: CR-002 enforces the UNION 0 < SLR <= 100 for every sludge type — the lower bound 0 is not printed anywhere and "up to 100" is printed only for easily settleable sludge, so WAS at SLR = 90 passes although Tab.1 prints 20-50 for it. Staged as three type-scoped gates.', verified_at=now() where id='130dc8fb-7ccb-40e2-b957-dbf2aca04824' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- TSS_thick
