-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- SECTION B — equations (4 rows) — QUOTE BACKFILL ONLY.
-- All four rows already carry verification_status='verified_against_standard' with
-- verification_quote = NULL. The guard is "verification_quote is null"; verification_status is NOT
-- written by these statements and keeps its existing value.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Eq.1 — eta (solids-related degree of separation), M381E-08
update public.equations set verification_quote='Calculation of the solids-related degree of separation: | \eta=\frac{\left(T S S_{\text {In }}-T S S_{\text {Ce }}\right) \cdot T S S_{\text {Dis }}}{\left(T S S_{\text {Dis }}-T S S_{\text {Ce }}\right) \cdot T S S_{\text {In }}} \cdot 100[\%] \tag{1} — printed p.7-8', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§2.1.10 Eq.1, printed p.7-8) [VC] — quote backfill only, status untouched. Dimensional check closes: (g/l x g/l)/(g/l x g/l) is dimensionless, x100 gives %. All three inputs are declared gTSS/l in the printed legend; the encoding stores TSS_In as kgTSS/m3 (numerically identical) and TSS_Ce/TSS_Dis as gTSS/l, so no scaling error. The formula is undefined at TSS_Dis = TSS_Ce (division by zero); no guard is encoded.', verified_at=now() where id='dec3bdb3-7578-45b5-86f6-7642c48790de' and verification_quote is null;

-- Eq.2 — A_thickener, M381E-03
update public.equations set verification_quote='When dimensioning continuous-flow gravity thickeners, the required surface $A_{\text {thickener }}\left[\mathrm{m}^{2}\right]$ is calculated by the added sludge quantity $Q_{\mathrm{s}}\left[\mathrm{m}^{3} / \mathrm{h}\right]$, the influent solids content $T S S_{\text {IN }}\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} / \mathrm{m}^{3}\right]$ and the solids loading rate SLR $\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} /\left(\mathrm{m}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{~d}\right)\right]$ selected from Table 1. | A_{\text {thickener }}=\frac{Q_{\mathrm{S}} \cdot T S S_{\mathrm{In}}}{\mathrm{SLR}} \quad\left[\mathrm{~m}^{2}\right] \tag{2} — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 Eq.2, printed p.16-17) [VC] — quote backfill only, status untouched. DIMENSIONAL CHECK FAILS AS PRINTED: m3/h x kgTSS/m3 / (kgTSS/(m2.d)) = m2 x d/h, not the printed [m2]. The equation closes only if the sludge quantity is taken per DAY (m3/d) or the solids loading rate per hour; with Q_s entered in the printed m3/h the resulting area is a factor 24 too small. The encoding reproduces the print faithfully (SR-1: no silent factor inserted); the ruling is staged in dwa-m-381e-STAGED-rulings.sql. Scope note: Eq.2 is printed for CONTINUOUS-flow gravity thickeners only.', verified_at=now() where id='2389029e-58e8-4174-a79e-ab3fbab89e7a' and verification_quote is null;

-- Eq.3 — H_S, M381E-03
update public.equations set verification_quote='The height of the sludge zone $H_{\mathrm{S}}[\mathrm{m}]$ is calculated using the solids loading rate SLR [kgTSS/ $\left(\mathrm{m}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{~d}\right)$ ], the solids content of the thickened sludge $\operatorname{TSS}_{\text {thick }}\left[\mathrm{kgTSS} / \mathrm{m}^{3}\right]$, and the detention time $t_{\mathrm{d}}[\mathrm{d}]$ of the sludge in the sludge zone: | H_{\mathrm{S}}=\frac{\mathrm{SLR} \cdot t_{\mathrm{d}}}{0,75 \cdot T S S_{\text {thick }}} \quad[\mathrm{m}] \tag{3} — printed p.16-17', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§4.1.2 Eq.3, printed p.16-17) [VC] — quote backfill only, status untouched. Dimensional check closes: kgTSS/(m2.d) x d / (kgTSS/m3) = m, matching the printed [m]. The dimensionless 0,75 is the printed "about 75 % of the final solids content of the thickened sludge" from the preceding sentence. Scope: continuous-flow gravity thickeners.', verified_at=now() where id='a09b565f-bfc8-4518-aac8-32ff38b2ebd9' and verification_quote is null;

-- Eq.4 — CRF, M381E-10
update public.equations set verification_quote='Investment costs were converted to annual costs using the equivalent annuity method and the capital recovery factor CRF | \mathrm{CRF}=\frac{i \cdot(1+i)^{\mathrm{n}}}{(1+i)^{\mathrm{n}}-1} \tag{4} — printed p.33', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§7 Eq.4, printed p.33) [VC] — quote backfill only, status untouched. Dimensional check closes: i is dimensionless and n is a pure exponent, so CRF is dimensionless ("factor" per Tab.10). i must be the DECIMAL rate; the worksheet also carries interest_rate in %, with no /100 conversion encoded — see the duplicate finding. CRF is undefined at i = 0. Its output is consumed by nothing downstream.', verified_at=now() where id='befaedbd-00da-4876-a951-e84f2d8cf185' and verification_quote is null;
